{"subjectId":"python","id":"stdlib-ds","title":"collections, heapq & bisect","group":"Data Structures","order":9,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">The standard-library data structures that turn O(n) interview solutions into O(1) or O(log n) ones.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-horizontal\"></i>deque — double-ended queue</h3>\n<p>O(1) appends and pops at <strong>both</strong> ends. Use it for queues (BFS) and sliding windows; a list's <code>pop(0)</code> is O(n).</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>from collections import deque\nq = deque([1, 2, 3])\nq.appendleft(0); q.append(4)\nprint(q.popleft(), q.pop(), list(q))    # 0 4 [1, 2, 3]\nwindow = deque(maxlen=3)                # keeps only the last 3 items\nfor x in range(6):\n    window.append(x)\nprint(list(window))                     # [3, 4, 5]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-chart-bar\"></i>Counter &amp; defaultdict</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>from collections import Counter, defaultdict\nc = Counter(\"mississippi\")\nprint(c.most_common(2))                  # [('i', 4), ('s', 4)]\n# Missing keys count as zero instead of raising KeyError:\nprint(c[\"z\"])                            # 0\n\ngraph = defaultdict(list)                # missing key → new empty list\nfor u, v in [(\"a\", \"b\"), (\"a\", \"c\"), (\"b\", \"c\")]:\n    graph[u].append(v)\nprint(dict(graph))                       # {'a': ['b', 'c'], 'b': ['c']}\n\ngroups = defaultdict(list)\nfor w in [\"eat\", \"tea\", \"tan\", \"ate\"]:\n    groups[\"\".join(sorted(w))].append(w)\nprint(list(groups.values()))             # [['eat', 'tea', 'ate'], ['tan']]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-stack-pop\"></i>heapq — priority queue</h3>\n<p>A <strong>min-heap</strong> stored in a plain list: <code>heappush</code> / <code>heappop</code> are O(log n), <code>heap[0]</code> is the minimum in O(1).</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import heapq\nnums = [5, 1, 8, 3, 2]\nheapq.heapify(nums)                       # O(n)\nheapq.heappush(nums, 0)\nprint(heapq.heappop(nums), nums[0])       # 0 1\nprint(heapq.nlargest(2, [5, 1, 8, 3]))    # [8, 5]\n\nmax_heap = []                             # no max-heap: store negatives\nfor x in [5, 1, 8]:\n    heapq.heappush(max_heap, -x)\nprint(-heapq.heappop(max_heap))           # 8\n\ntasks = [(2, \"write\"), (1, \"plan\"), (3, \"ship\")]\nheapq.heapify(tasks)                      # tuples compare by first item\nprint(heapq.heappop(tasks))               # (1, 'plan')</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>If priorities tie, tuples fall back to comparing the next item — which may not be comparable. Add a counter: <code>(priority, count, item)</code>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-binary\"></i>bisect — binary search on sorted lists</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import bisect\nxs = [1, 3, 3, 5, 8]\nprint(bisect.bisect_left(xs, 3), bisect.bisect_right(xs, 3))   # 1 3\nbisect.insort(xs, 4)                                          # insert, keep sorted\nprint(xs)                                                     # [1, 3, 3, 4, 5, 8]</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>Use</th><th>Key operations</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>FIFO queue / BFS</td><td><code>deque</code></td><td><code>append</code>, <code>popleft</code> — O(1)</td></tr><tr><td>Counting</td><td><code>Counter</code></td><td><code>most_common(k)</code>, arithmetic between counters</td></tr><tr><td>Grouping / adjacency list</td><td><code>defaultdict(list)</code></td><td>auto-creates missing keys</td></tr><tr><td>k smallest / Dijkstra / scheduling</td><td><code>heapq</code></td><td><code>heappush</code>, <code>heappop</code> — O(log n)</td></tr><tr><td>Search in sorted data</td><td><code>bisect</code></td><td><code>bisect_left</code> — O(log n)</td></tr><tr><td>LRU-style ordering</td><td><code>OrderedDict</code></td><td><code>move_to_end</code>, <code>popitem(last=False)</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>"}